<title>GERMANY: France's Arthuis hopes current forex rates last.</title>
<headline>France's Arthuis hopes current forex rates last.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Finance Minister Jean Arthuis said on Saturday he hopes that current exchange rate levels would be stable and lasting.</p>
<p>&quot;I think that the recent appreciation in the dollar was logical and necessary,&quot; he told reporters as he arrived for a one day meeting of the seven most industrialised nations.</p>
<p>&quot;I would like the new configuration of exchange rates to be stable and lasting,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The U.S. Germany, Japan, France, Italy, Canada and Britain are members of the G7.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
